From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Keyboard firmware screen and *#*#1122#*#* on the Q25

The stock Zinwa Q25 menu behind *#*#1122#*#* (Turn off, Firmware
upgrade, Exit) is not in LineageOS, so a keyboard firmware update meant
returning to stock. The bbqX0kbd driver keeps its switch,
/proc/firmware_upgrade (1 off, 2 download mode with USB handed to the
keyboard, 0 back to normal), so Settings drives it:

- SableKeyboardFirmwareActivity: the three steps as buttons (download
  only after off; Exit always), touch only because the keyboard is off;
  kept through the keyboard's own disconnect, and finishing the screen
  in any other step writes 0 so the keyboard and USB come back.
- SableKeyboardFirmwareCodeReceiver: *#*#1122#*#* opens it (owner user,
  MODIFY_PHONE_STATE sender only).
- Settings > System > Keyboard > Keyboard firmware, searchable, shown
  only where /proc/firmware_upgrade exists.

Needs the device sepolicy that lets system_app write the node.
